2 0 obj
<<
/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (A\040Bit\040Level\040Representation\040for\040Time\040Series\040Data\040Mining\040with\040Shape\040Based\040Similarity)
/Author (Anthony\040J\056\040Bagnall\054\040Chotirat\040Ann\040Ratanamahatana\054\040Eamonn\040Keogh\054\040Stefano\040Lonardi\054\040G\056\040J\056\040Janacek)
/Subject (Clipping\040is\040the\040process\040of\040transforming\040a\040real\040valued\040series\040into\040a\040sequence\040of\040bits\040representing\040whether\040each\040data\040is\040above\040or\040below\040the\040average\056\040In\040this\040paper\054\040we\040argue\040that\040clipping\040is\040a\040useful\040and\040flexible\040transformation\040for\040the\040exploratory\040analysis\040of\040large\040time\040dependent\040data\040sets\056\040We\040demonstrate\040how\040time\040series\040stored\040as\040bits\040can\040be\040very\040efficiently\040compressed\040and\040manipulated\040and\040that\054\040under\040some\040assumptions\054\040the\040discriminatory\040power\040with\040clipped\040series\040is\040asymptotically\040equivalent\040to\040that\040achieved\040with\040the\040raw\040data\056\040Unlike\040other\040transformations\054\040clipped\040series\040can\040be\040compared\040directly\040to\040the\040raw\040data\040series\056\040We\040show\040that\040this\040means\040we\040can\040form\040a\040tight\040lower\040bounding\040metric\040for\040Euclidean\040and\040Dynamic\040Time\040Warping\040distance\040and\040hence\040efficiently\040query\040by\040content\056\040Clipped\040data\040can\040be\040used\040in\040conjunction\040with\040a\040host\040of\040algorithms\040and\040statistical\040tests\040that\040naturally\040follow\040from\040the\040binary\040nature\040of\040the\040data\056\040A\040series\040of\040experiments\040illustrate\040how\040clipped\040series\040can\040be\040used\040in\040increasingly\040complex\040ways\040to\040achieve\040better\040results\040than\040other\040popular\040representations\056\040The\040usefulness\040of\040the\040proposed\040representation\040is\040demonstrated\040by\040the\040fact\040that\040the\040results\040with\040clipped\040data\040are\040consistently\040better\040than\040those\040achieved\040with\040a\040Wavelet\040or\040Discrete\040Fourier\040Transformation\040at\040the\040same\040compression\040ratio\040for\040both\040clustering\040and\040query\040by\040content\056\040The\040flexibility\040of\040the\040representation\040is\040shown\040by\040the\040fact\040that\040we\040can\040take\040advantage\040of\040a\040variable\040Run\040Length\040Encoding\040of\040clipped\040series\040to\040define\040an\040approximation\040of\040the\040Kolmogorov\040complexity\040and\040hence\040perform\040Kolmogorov\040based\040clustering\056)
/Keywords (01\040Jul\0402006\054\040Data\040Mining\040and\040Knowledge\040Discovery\054\040Clipping\040\050photography\051\054\040Cluster\040analysis\054\040Series\040\050mathematics\051\054\040Run\055length\040encoding\054\040Transformation\040\050function\051\054\040University\040of\040East\040Anglia\054\040Chulalongkorn\040University\054\040University\040of\040California\054\040Riverside)
>>
endobj
